    for start, end in sorted_intervals:
        if start == end:
            continue
        if result and start <= result[-1][1]:
            if end > result[-1][1]:
                result[-1] = (result[-1][0], end)
        else:
            result.append((start, end))
    return result

Note: touching intervals merged means start <= prev_end. Empty intervals (start==end) discarded. Validate start > end raises ValueError. Don't mutate input — sorted() copies. Tuples are immutable anyway.
